From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 23:57:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/34] x23: batch 1024, group_size 16

1024/16 = 64 GRPO groups per step, against 32 at the previous 256/8. Larger
groups also tighten the within-group advantage estimate, which is where the
noise was: over 36 steps at 256/8 reward std was 0.039 against a total linear
trend of +0.013.

Trade-off worth noting: 64 groups means 64 distinct prompts per step versus
128 at 1024/8, so prompt diversity per step drops while per-group advantage
quality rises.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017wiESxhziDrnsLnG9aizTd
---
 configs/china/orchestrator.x23.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/configs/china/orchestrator.x23.toml b/configs/china/orchestrator.x23.toml
index ceb59e1..cb528c6 100644
--- a/configs/china/orchestrator.x23.toml
+++ b/configs/china/orchestrator.x23.toml
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@ output_dir = "/data/glm52-rl/runs/x23/run_x23"
 max_steps = 200
 seq_len = 16384
 batch_size = 1024
-group_size = 8
+group_size = 16
 max_inflight_rollouts = 1024
 # 4, not 2: batches go out over ZMQ fire-and-forget, so a trainer restart
 # loses whatever was in flight. With a tight cap the orchestrator then holds
